From 6d7a2fb475f8f0b8874147f9ead6abe2381711a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mptfire <263163432+mptfire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:12:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] config: the overlay may only tighten, never de-escalate

A cloned repo could name full_access as the starting mode, stand the
bash sandbox down, or open the private-fetch gate: all three sat below
the user's config, so a checkout shipped its own guardrail settings and
nothing flagged them. Posture a repo may suggest stays posture that
only tightens: default_mode clamps to accept_edits at the ceiling,
sandbox_bash stands down to the default when it says off, and
allow_private_fetch is gone from the overlay (the key warns as
unrecognized in repos that still carry it). The user's file outranks
everything as before; DESIGN.md says the same thing now.
---
 DESIGN.md            |  12 ++--
 gertie/src/config.rs | 166 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 2 files changed, 136 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

